    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **69 tests run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final org.slf4j.Logger NOTIFY = org.slf4j.LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome line** in `addOwner`, right after the owner is saved and the audit events are logged (so it only fires on a genuine successful create, not on the idempotent-replay or any validation-rejection path):\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome notification enqueued: ownerId={} memberId={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThe line carries both the owner id and the unified `memberId`, which is exactly what `Cp57Tests` asserts via `notify.anyContains(String.valueOf(id), memberId)`. Placing it after `saveOwner` guarantees `owner.getId()` is populated and the `memberId` is the deduplicated, stored value returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
